    "endpoint": "New raw-data reduction of unstitched scan monitor-normalized ratios using one direct exposure per angle and pinned fixed detector center and width measured on the corresponding direct beam. Scale one, background subtraction, 2.8–18Å wavelength, 3.4% rebin. Includes every original 56 bins per scan, negative and >1 ratios retained.",
    "forecast_design": "Nine opaque copies first received direct reference histograms in place of all physical reflected histograms, and corresponding surrogate count summaries before author instrument reduction. Real per-scan geometry retained. 504 q/FWHM values refrozen; measured extraction must reproduce these coordinates at rtol=1e-11/atol=1e-13 or refuse without rescaling.",
    "absolute_limit": "Detector registration aperture, direct/reference date and unknown actual SLD/gain can change observed ratios. They are not calibrated independent reflectivity truth."
  },
